12:["$","$L11","054",{"a":{"id":"054","slug":"viral-hit","term":"Viral Hit","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"viral-hit","tier":"canonical","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["viral-hit-rate","evidence-ladder","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Viral compared with what?","dek":"A Viral Hit is an unusually high distribution outcome relative to a defined baseline: account, cohort or campaign.","point":"A Viral Hit is an unusually high distribution outcome relative to a defined baseline: account, cohort or campaign. A fixed view threshold does not fit every context.","body":["A 40,000-view video means different things for an account usually reaching 600 and one usually reaching 500,000. These numbers are illustrative. Define the baseline before observing results. Otherwise you can move the threshold until it supports the story you wanted.","Keep the selected threshold and its rationale beside the result. A history-relative threshold can become unstable when an account has published very little. A comparable cohort may then be more informative, provided its composition is justified. The word viral should remain attached to a readable baseline. If no credible reference exists yet, describe the observed views and uncertainty rather than forcing a classification."],"action":["Choose a comparable historical baseline.","Set the threshold before reading results."],"trap":"A view spike is not proof of commercial impact.","quote":"Viral compared with what?","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Viral compared with what?","text":"A Viral Hit is an unusually high distribution outcome relative to a defined baseline: account, cohort or campaign.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Viral Hit","text":"A Viral Hit is an unusually high distribution outcome relative to a defined baseline: account, cohort or campaign. A fixed view threshold does not fit every context.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A view spike is not proof of commercial impact.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Choose a comparable historical baseline.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Set the threshold before reading results.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/viral-hit.jpg","width":1280,"height":691,"alt":{"en":"A powerful ocean wave bursts into white spray against a rocky shoreline."},"credit":"Ronnie Robertson","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 778899c2be915c2aeae6bf20fe3ab48071988fdf.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burgi_Wave_Burst_IMG_7243_(16591566349).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
13:["$","$L11","055",{"a":{"id":"055","slug":"viral-hit-rate","term":"Viral Hit Rate","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"viral-hit-rate","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["median-vs-mean","viral-hit","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The denominator is half the story.","dek":"Viral Hit Rate is the proportion of eligible posts exceeding a predefined outlier threshold.","point":"Viral Hit Rate is the proportion of eligible posts exceeding a predefined outlier threshold. Interpretation depends on threshold, cohort and window.","body":["In a fictional example, four hits among one hundred eligible posts yield 4%. If twenty more are too recent to evaluate, show them separately. Do not silently add them to the denominator. Retain uncertainty too: four events offer limited stability for predicting the next series.","Also display results by creative concept. Ten versions of one idea do not represent ten independent discoveries. Post-level rate answers a production question; concept-level rate helps describe creative discovery. Both can be useful, but should not merge into one unexplained score. Keeping their denominators separate prevents a heavily repeated successful idea from being mistaken for a pipeline that repeatedly discovers unrelated winners."],"action":["Publish threshold, window and exclusions.","Show absolute counts beside the rate."],"trap":"Comparing rates with different eligibility criteria can mislead.","quote":"The denominator is half the story.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The denominator is half the story.","text":"Viral Hit Rate is the proportion of eligible posts exceeding a predefined outlier threshold.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit-rate.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Viral Hit Rate","text":"Viral Hit Rate is the proportion of eligible posts exceeding a predefined outlier threshold. Interpretation depends on threshold, cohort and window.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit-rate.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Comparing rates with different eligibility criteria can mislead.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit-rate.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Publish threshold, window and exclusions.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit-rate.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Show absolute counts beside the rate.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/viral-hit-rate.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/viral-hit-rate.jpg","width":1280,"height":854,"alt":{"en":"Raindrops cling to a car window, blurring the parked vehicles outside."},"credit":"Shixart1985","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: b2960be3a0274e5d5f571933bde8e653e6b20033.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Close-up_of_the_rain_drops_on_a_car_window._Car_in_a_blurry_background.jpg","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
14:["$","$L11","056",{"a":{"id":"056","slug":"median-vs-mean","term":"Median vs mean","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"median-vs-mean","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["percentiles","viral-hit-rate","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The average loves an overly good story.","dek":"The mean adds values and divides by their count.","point":"The mean adds values and divides by their count. The median describes the middle of a sorted series. They answer different questions.","body":["Fictional example: 100, 100, 100, 100 and 10,000 views. The mean is 2,080; the median is 100. The first describes theoretically spread volume; the second identifies the central post. Keep both alongside the distribution to distinguish an isolated hit from broad improvement.","In the example, removing the 10,000-view result brings the mean down to 100. This sensitivity check does not mean the hit should be discarded. It reveals dependence on one observation. A useful report keeps the complete result and context, then asks about repeatability rather than inventing it. The exceptional post may matter greatly while still telling us little about what an ordinary next post will achieve."],"action":["Show mean and median together.","Inspect extreme values."],"trap":"The median can also hide the economic importance of a few very large outcomes.","quote":"The average loves an overly good story.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The average loves an overly good story.","text":"The mean adds values and divides by their count.","media":"/images/editorial/median-vs-mean.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Median vs mean","text":"The mean adds values and divides by their count. The median describes the middle of a sorted series. They answer different questions.","media":"/images/editorial/median-vs-mean.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"The median can also hide the economic importance of a few very large outcomes.","media":"/images/editorial/median-vs-mean.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Show mean and median together.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/median-vs-mean.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Inspect extreme values.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/median-vs-mean.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/median-vs-mean.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"Smooth, multicolored pebbles packed together on a beach."},"credit":"Quim Gil","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 87bd342bb93763993e78d946b54b3bf395b1b570.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pebbles_in_Rethymno%27s_beach.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
15:["$","$L11","057",{"a":{"id":"057","slug":"percentiles","term":"Distribution percentiles","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"percentiles","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["power-law","median-vs-mean","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"P90 is not a new word for good.","dek":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution.","point":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution. P90 describes its upper region but depends on cohort size and definition.","body":["A percentile across ten posts is less stable than it looks on a dashboard. State the calculation method if tools disagree. Compare equally mature series and keep counts visible. A percentile describes observations; it does not guarantee future performance.","When reading change, show several points in the distribution. A stable median with a stronger upper region tells a different story from broad improvement. The first may suggest more positive extremes, but their cause remains to be understood. These summaries should open the content analysis rather than replace it. Show the same observation window and calculation method so apparent movement is not a reporting artifact."],"action":["Document the calculation convention.","Show each cohort’s size."],"trap":"A high percentile in a small series is not a reliable forecast.","quote":"P90 is not a new word for good.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"P90 is not a new word for good.","text":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution.","media":"/images/editorial/percentiles.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Distribution percentiles","text":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution. P90 describes its upper region but depends on cohort size and definition.","media":"/images/editorial/percentiles.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A high percentile in a small series is not a reliable forecast.","media":"/images/editorial/percentiles.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Document the calculation convention.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/percentiles.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Show each cohort’s size.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/percentiles.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/percentiles.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"Layers of mountain ridges fade into blue haze beneath the distant Himalayas."},"credit":"Timothy A. Gonsalves","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 709838554486b27f57f1ad25af603f9799cbbb14.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shivaliks_Himalayas_Aerial_Dehaze_Himachal_Feb20_R16_02827.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
16:["$","$L11","058",{"a":{"id":"058","slug":"power-law","term":"Distribution concentration","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"power-law","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["top-ten-accounts","percentiles","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The hit makes noise. The rest explains the system.","dek":"Concentration measures the share of outcomes produced by a fraction of posts.","point":"Concentration measures the share of outcomes produced by a fraction of posts. An unequal distribution is not automatically evidence of a power law.","body":["Calculate the share of views from top posts, then inspect the rest. If one post carries nearly everything, total volume is fragile. That can still be viable if cost and repeatability are understood. Describing concentration beats attaching an untested mathematical label.","A ranked contribution chart often makes concentration visible without fitting a theoretical curve. Add counts and the observation window. Actually testing a power law requires a dedicated statistical method and comparison with alternative models. The expression should not decorate an outcome that is merely unequal. Descriptive reporting can still guide allocation well when it clearly shows which posts contribute and how much uncertainty remains about future repetition."],"action":["Measure the share carried by top posts.","Show results with and without the largest hit."],"trap":"Removing an outlier to improve the average’s story may erase an essential part of the phenomenon.","quote":"The hit makes noise. The rest explains the system.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The hit makes noise. The rest explains the system.","text":"Concentration measures the share of outcomes produced by a fraction of posts.","media":"/images/editorial/power-law.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Distribution concentration","text":"Concentration measures the share of outcomes produced by a fraction of posts. An unequal distribution is not automatically evidence of a power law.","media":"/images/editorial/power-law.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Removing an outlier to improve the average’s story may erase an essential part of the phenomenon.","media":"/images/editorial/power-law.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Measure the share carried by top posts.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/power-law.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Show results with and without the largest hit.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/power-law.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/power-law.jpg","width":1280,"height":720,"alt":{"en":"Lightning illuminates a storm cloud above a harbour pier and lighthouse."},"credit":"Maxime Raynal","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 74ed3615cd6743fb4e031d1d1b58a3fd45de2d23.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
17:["$","$L11","059",{"a":{"id":"059","slug":"top-ten-accounts","term":"Account concentration","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"top-ten-accounts","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["matched-cohorts","power-law","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The network works. Or one account carries it.","dek":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome.","point":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome. It complements post-level analysis by revealing structural dependence.","body":["Sum eligible outcomes by account over one window and rank contributions. Compare publishing volumes too: one account may dominate because it receives most resources. Ask whether that allocation reflects observed quality or operational habit.","For illustration, an account receiving half the creative work also produces half the views. Its volume dominance does not necessarily mean greater efficiency. Another, less supplied account may produce more outcome per resource. Compare those views while retaining differences in purpose and assigned creative quality. A portfolio decision needs both total contribution and a fair description of what each account was given a chance to do."],"action":["Compare contributions with allocated resources.","Record accounts with insufficient data."],"trap":"Low contribution does not prove an account is useless when its purpose differs.","quote":"The network works. Or one account carries it.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The network works. Or one account carries it.","text":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome.","media":"/images/editorial/top-ten-accounts.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Account concentration","text":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome. It complements post-level analysis by revealing structural dependence.","media":"/images/editorial/top-ten-accounts.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Low contribution does not prove an account is useless when its purpose differs.","media":"/images/editorial/top-ten-accounts.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Compare contributions with allocated resources.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/top-ten-accounts.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Record accounts with insufficient data.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/top-ten-accounts.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/top-ten-accounts.jpg","width":1280,"height":832,"alt":{"en":"The illuminated Price Building rises above surrounding rooftops in Quebec City at night."},"credit":"Wilfredor","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 806daa0796b8e1901acf5837aa1c26d99194be81.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Price_Building_illuminated_at_night_in_Quebec_City.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
18:["$","$L11","060",{"a":{"id":"060","slug":"matched-cohorts","term":"Matched cohorts","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"matched-cohorts","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["posting-time-myth","top-ten-accounts","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Compare what is actually comparable.","dek":"A matched cohort aligns observations on known characteristics.","point":"A matched cohort aligns observations on known characteristics. It reduces some visible differences without automatically eliminating all confounding.","body":["For publishing-method comparisons, start with format, market, account age and measurement window. Retain unmatched cases separately rather than forcing implausible pairs. Unobserved variables remain a limitation. A matched comparison must explain group credibility, not merely display a gap.","Record excluded cases and their characteristics. If only the easiest accounts to compare remain, conclusions may not apply to the full network. A reproducible method lets another reader understand the population actually covered. Transparency about limits is more useful than presenting a selected sample as universal. The comparison can remain valuable, provided the claim stays inside the boundaries of the observations that support it."],"action":["Choose matching variables before analysis.","Publish exclusions and coverage."],"trap":"Matching is not randomization and does not establish causality by itself.","quote":"Compare what is actually comparable.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Compare what is actually comparable.","text":"A matched cohort aligns observations on known characteristics.","media":"/images/editorial/matched-cohorts.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Matched cohorts","text":"A matched cohort aligns observations on known characteristics. It reduces some visible differences without automatically eliminating all confounding.","media":"/images/editorial/matched-cohorts.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Matching is not randomization and does not establish causality by itself.","media":"/images/editorial/matched-cohorts.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Choose matching variables before analysis.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/matched-cohorts.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Publish exclusions and coverage.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/matched-cohorts.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/matched-cohorts.jpg","width":1280,"height":869,"alt":{"en":"A regular grid of windows covers the facade of the Conjunto Nacional building in São Paulo."},"credit":"Wilfredor","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 31c63c97787fe7ffbaeaa9334ac163366f311fbc.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Facade_of_the_Conjunto_Nacional_cropped_version.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
19:["$","$L11","061",{"a":{"id":"061","slug":"posting-time-myth","term":"Posting-time myth","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"posting-time-myth","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["posting-frequency","matched-cohorts","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"7:42 p.m. is not a strategy.","dek":"Posting-time effects may depend on audience and context.","point":"Posting-time effects may depend on audience and context. A universally optimal time is not demonstrated in this protocol.","body":["Allocate comparable content across predefined windows without reserving your strongest topics for a favorite slot. Measure at equal post ages. Separate weekday and local time if the sample supports that detail. Keep the verdict unknown until the test is run and analyzed.","Plan what happens if no clear difference appears. The team might choose the easiest window to operate and spend saved effort on creative work. That would still be useful information. An experiment does not need to uncover a spectacular trick to improve operations. Recording this decision beforehand prevents a null or uncertain outcome from being hidden simply because it does not support an exciting optimization headline."],"action":["Preregister time windows.","Distribute concepts across them."],"trap":"A screenshot of success at one time cannot identify the best posting time.","quote":"7:42 p.m. is not a strategy.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"7:42 p.m. is not a strategy.","text":"Posting-time effects may depend on audience and context.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-time-myth.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Posting-time myth","text":"Posting-time effects may depend on audience and context. A universally optimal time is not demonstrated in this protocol.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-time-myth.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A screenshot of success at one time cannot identify the best posting time.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-time-myth.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Preregister time windows.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-time-myth.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Distribute concepts across them.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-time-myth.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/posting-time-myth.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"A close view of the ornate blue and gold Prague Astronomical Clock."},"credit":"Jorge Royan","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 39d974a96d456e41bea4f010599f4a383ce7d3cc.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Prague_Astronomical_Clock_in_Old_Town_-_8559.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1a:["$","$L11","062",{"a":{"id":"062","slug":"posting-frequency","term":"Posting frequency","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"posting-frequency","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["warming-study","posting-time-myth","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Posting more: more chances or more noise?","dek":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load.","point":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load. Higher totals can coexist with weaker individual posts.","body":["Define two realistic cadences with comparable creative quality. Observe coordination costs and undelivered content. Do not conclude from average views alone: the network may seek more qualified visits at a manageable cost. No test result is supplied here.","A favorable total may also increase team fatigue or correction work. Record those effects in the review instead of treating them as outside the experiment. A suitable cadence depends on the whole system. Sustainable output with readable briefs may be preferable to a production spike that cannot survive the following week. This is an operating tradeoff to evaluate, not an assumption that lower frequency always performs better."],"action":["Set cadence, duration and primary metric.","Track total cost and per-post outcomes."],"trap":"Changing cadence and quality together prevents isolating frequency effects.","quote":"Posting more: more chances or more noise?","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Posting more: more chances or more noise?","text":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-frequency.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Posting frequency","text":"A frequency test must separate total volume, per-post performance and production load. Higher totals can coexist with weaker individual posts.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-frequency.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Changing cadence and quality together prevents isolating frequency effects.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-frequency.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Set cadence, duration and primary metric.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-frequency.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Track total cost and per-post outcomes.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/posting-frequency.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/posting-frequency.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"Illuminated buttons and rows of faders on a sound mixing console."},"credit":"Lchader","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: f656480410fd8f0e9890bb89a24528a9f4148722.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Audio_mixer_close_up.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1b:["$","$L11","063",{"a":{"id":"063","slug":"warming-study","term":"Warming protocol","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"warming-study","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["account-age","posting-frequency","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Warming deserves more than an anecdote.","dek":"A warming protocol compares preparations defined before publishing.","point":"A warming protocol compares preparations defined before publishing. It should separate niche learning, account behavior and later outcomes.","body":["Plan comparable groups: general preparation, targeted preparation and control where suitable. Keep creative criteria and measurement age consistent. Define possible outcomes, including no difference. This document proposes a method; it does not claim an executed experiment.","Separate observations made during preparation from those collected after publishing. The first can show improved niche understanding without proving a distribution effect. Keeping these benefits distinct avoids an all-or-nothing verdict. The practice may support creative research even when a reach test remains inconclusive. Describe exactly which benefit was observed so a practical learning outcome does not silently become a claim about platform recommendation behavior."],"action":["Describe preparations precisely.","Plan handling of dropouts and missing data."],"trap":"A favorable observation does not establish that warming caused the result.","quote":"Warming deserves more than an anecdote.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Warming deserves more than an anecdote.","text":"A warming protocol compares preparations defined before publishing.","media":"/images/editorial/warming-study.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Warming protocol","text":"A warming protocol compares preparations defined before publishing. It should separate niche learning, account behavior and later outcomes.","media":"/images/editorial/warming-study.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A favorable observation does not establish that warming caused the result.","media":"/images/editorial/warming-study.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Describe preparations precisely.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/warming-study.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Plan handling of dropouts and missing data.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/warming-study.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/warming-study.jpg","width":1280,"height":811,"alt":{"en":"An elevated view of the glass greenhouse at Jevremovac Botanical Garden in Belgrade."},"credit":"Petar Milošević","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: bf57161b64196cd44da49bbcf409196ab2c904fd.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A1%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%9A%D0%B0%D0%BA,_%D0%91%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%B1%D0%B0%D1%88%D1%82%D0%B0_%D0%88%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BC%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%86_(greenhouse_Jevremovac_Botanical_Garden,_Belgrade,_Serbia).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1c:["$","$L11","064",{"a":{"id":"064","slug":"account-age","term":"Account age","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"account-age","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["slideshow-vs-video","warming-study","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"An old account is not a control group.","dek":"Account age can be associated with history, followers and behavior.","point":"Account age can be associated with history, followers and behavior. Comparing old and new accounts requires distinguishing those dimensions.","body":["An old account without recent activity is not equivalent to an established creator. Describe age, activity, audience and observable restriction history. Choose categories before searching for the split yielding the prettiest gap. Without comparable data, the verdict remains open.","If older accounts are the only ones surviving several cycles, they have already passed through selection. That history may explain part of their difference from new accounts. Keep cohort exits and inactive periods. Age is a convenient variable, but it does not summarize everything an account experienced. A credible analysis should resist treating a date field as a complete description of operational history and accumulated audience context."],"action":["Separate age from activity.","Account for available audience differences."],"trap":"Correlation with age may reflect selection among surviving accounts.","quote":"An old account is not a control group.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"An old account is not a control group.","text":"Account age can be associated with history, followers and behavior.","media":"/images/editorial/account-age.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Account age","text":"Account age can be associated with history, followers and behavior. Comparing old and new accounts requires distinguishing those dimensions.","media":"/images/editorial/account-age.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Correlation with age may reflect selection among surviving accounts.","media":"/images/editorial/account-age.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Separate age from activity.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/account-age.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Account for available audience differences.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/account-age.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/account-age.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"Growth rings and age markers across the cut trunk of an ancient tree."},"credit":"Thomas Quine","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 3daa3fc306039c48b7c0987c6b2b0724b8689c3b.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tree_rings_of_1500_year_old_tree.ARW_(23821647991).jpg","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1d:["$","$L11","065",{"a":{"id":"065","slug":"slideshow-vs-video","term":"Slideshow vs video","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"slideshow-vs-video","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["formatted-vs-chaotic","account-age","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Slideshow versus video: context comes first.","dek":"Comparing slideshow and video requires a comparable promise and audience.","point":"Comparing slideshow and video requires a comparable promise and audience. Reading behavior and available metrics may differ between formats.","body":["Turn one question into two suitable treatments without forcing video into an animated slideshow. Choose a useful shared metric, such as measurable qualified visits. Keep format-native metrics separate. The test compares content experiences, not file extensions.","Include production cost in the table. A video may achieve a stronger raw outcome with much more work, while a slideshow may make an explanation easier to revise. The choice depends on the editorial question and resources. Present the tradeoff rather than crowning a format for every situation. Also retain whether both treatments actually delivered equivalent information; unequal substance can otherwise masquerade as a format effect."],"action":["Keep the same user question.","Choose an interpretable shared measure."],"trap":"Comparing differently defined completion rates can manufacture a winner.","quote":"Slideshow versus video: context comes first.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Slideshow versus video: context comes first.","text":"Comparing slideshow and video requires a comparable promise and audience.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-vs-video.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Slideshow vs video","text":"Comparing slideshow and video requires a comparable promise and audience. Reading behavior and available metrics may differ between formats.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-vs-video.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Comparing differently defined completion rates can manufacture a winner.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-vs-video.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Keep the same user question.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-vs-video.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Choose an interpretable shared measure.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/slideshow-vs-video.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/slideshow-vs-video.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"A strip of 8 mm film curls away from its reel."},"credit":"Coyau","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 5002c79b0b2e3888e3004386bf9c24c987c10f2c.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:8_mm_Kodak_safety_film_reel_06.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1e:["$","$L11","066",{"a":{"id":"066","slug":"formatted-vs-chaotic","term":"Formatted vs chaotic","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"formatted-vs-chaotic","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["creative-diversity-test","slideshow-vs-video","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Series or chaos? A test, not a taste war.","dek":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats.","point":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats. It needs a shared editorial objective and documented variation.","body":["A series may improve operating consistency; a flexible account may explore more angles. Measure creative workload and concepts tested too. Otherwise you may compare a well-resourced system with an underfunded one. This protocol presumes no winner.","Archive the concepts actually published in each group. A chaotic account may appear stronger because it received the best subjects. A series may appear more stable because its variations were less ambitious. A creative record makes these differences discussable instead of hiding them behind a format label. The result should explain the tested systems, not imply that one loosely defined category has defeated another in every possible context."],"action":["Define fixed elements in each group.","Compare invested resources."],"trap":"One campaign’s outcome does not become a universal rule about formats.","quote":"Series or chaos? A test, not a taste war.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Series or chaos? A test, not a taste war.","text":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Formatted vs chaotic","text":"A Formatted versus Chaotic test compares a recurring structure with multiple formats. It needs a shared editorial objective and documented variation.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"One campaign’s outcome does not become a universal rule about formats.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define fixed elements in each group.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Compare invested resources.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/formatted-vs-chaotic.jpg","width":1280,"height":843,"alt":{"en":"An upward view through the sweeping spiral staircase at the Vatican Museums."},"credit":"Colin","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 26b9dc66ea2c1b295e5c1834a652b763214cad24.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vatican_Museums_Spiral_Staircase_Looking_Up_2012.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
1f:["$","$L11","067",{"a":{"id":"067","slug":"creative-diversity-test","term":"Creative diversity","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"creative-diversity-test","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["native-features-test","formatted-vs-chaotic","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Diversity also lives in what you learn.","dek":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files.","point":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files. It connects concepts with outcomes and their stability.","body":["Label angles, personas and situations before examining performance. Compare similar-volume groups with documented diversity differences. Keep costs visible: more angles may require more design work. Ask whether the difference improves useful learning, not merely outcome dispersion.","A blind review can help: hide results and ask several people to classify creative work using the taxonomy. Disagreements expose vague categories. This does not measure marketing impact, but checks whether the definition of diversity can be applied without already knowing winners. Keep ambiguous cases visible and revise the coding guide before using those categories to explain performance or allocate the next production budget."],"action":["Define a simple creative taxonomy.","Measure outcomes and design effort."],"trap":"A taxonomy invented after reading results can rationalize successes.","quote":"Diversity also lives in what you learn.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Diversity also lives in what you learn.","text":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Creative diversity","text":"A creative-diversity test examines meaningful variation rather than counting files. It connects concepts with outcomes and their stability.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A taxonomy invented after reading results can rationalize successes.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define a simple creative taxonomy.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Measure outcomes and design effort.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/creative-diversity-test.jpg","width":1280,"height":676,"alt":{"en":"Colorful figures and decorative panels in a stained glass cathedral window."},"credit":"Pudelek; retouch by Albertus teolog","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: ab2b78f70b4197eba0649f9c964509668fa28271.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St_Vitus_Cathedral_-_Stained_glass_(retouch).jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
20:["$","$L11","068",{"a":{"id":"068","slug":"native-features-test","term":"Native features","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"native-features-test","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["zero-view-rate","creative-diversity-test","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Maybe it is not native. Maybe it is the feature.","dek":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel.","point":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel. Comparing whole workflows does not always allow that separation.","body":["If one group uses audio or formatting absent from the other, treatment no longer concerns upload method alone. Document features precisely. Depending on the question, accept that bundle of differences or design a narrower test. State honestly what the comparison measures.","A protocol may deliberately compare two complete experiences when that is the team’s actual decision. Name the treatment accordingly. The aim is not to remove all complexity but to avoid a narrow conclusion from a broad test. Keep the result’s wording at the scale of what changed. A workflow comparison can be practically useful without identifying the isolated contribution of every feature inside it."],"action":["Inventory feature differences.","Choose a feature test or a workflow test."],"trap":"A gap between workflows does not identify which component produced the effect.","quote":"Maybe it is not native. Maybe it is the feature.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Maybe it is not native. Maybe it is the feature.","text":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Native features","text":"A native-feature test separates a feature’s effect from its publishing channel. Comparing whole workflows does not always allow that separation.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A gap between workflows does not identify which component produced the effect.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Inventory feature differences.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Choose a feature test or a workflow test.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/native-features-test.jpg","width":1280,"height":824,"alt":{"en":"Camera lenses of different sizes and focal lengths arranged on a shelf."},"credit":"Carlos Valenzuela Montuy","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 64ce48e9dc3b2aa2cc7497d42862acec291b1373.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Photographic_lenses_and_tubes_2025.jpg","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
21:["$","$L11","069",{"a":{"id":"069","slug":"zero-view-rate","term":"Zero-view rate","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"zero-view-rate","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["confidence-intervals","native-features-test","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A zero rate deserves a complete definition.","dek":"Zero-view rate depends on observation age, measurement source and eligibility scope.","point":"Zero-view rate depends on observation age, measurement source and eligibility scope. Missing data must remain separate.","body":["Count genuinely published posts observable at the selected window. Separate null values, collection failures and posts too young to evaluate. Show raw counts. A rate declining because a tool no longer retrieves problematic accounts does not necessarily indicate improvement.","Check collection before raising a performance alert. If several accounts lose data simultaneously, the problem may sit in the measurement tool. Preserve useful technical responses and the last valid observation. This avoids launching editorial fixes for a counter that simply was not refreshed. The operational next step should follow the evidence available, while the actual distribution outcome remains unknown until a reliable observation can be made."],"action":["Set observation age and source.","Keep an unknown-data category."],"trap":"Observed zero, missing zero and assumed zero are not interchangeable.","quote":"A zero rate deserves a complete definition.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A zero rate deserves a complete definition.","text":"Zero-view rate depends on observation age, measurement source and eligibility scope.","media":"/images/editorial/zero-view-rate.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Zero-view rate","text":"Zero-view rate depends on observation age, measurement source and eligibility scope. Missing data must remain separate.","media":"/images/editorial/zero-view-rate.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Observed zero, missing zero and assumed zero are not interchangeable.","media":"/images/editorial/zero-view-rate.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Set observation age and source.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/zero-view-rate.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Keep an unknown-data category.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/zero-view-rate.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/zero-view-rate.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"An empty swimming pool stands beside rubble at a demolished motel."},"credit":"Michael Rivera","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: f4de30510a8975e36ee0c17fdab5f9935d2799bb.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empty_swimming_pool_in_front_of_demolished_Western_Motel,_Valdosta.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
22:["$","$L11","070",{"a":{"id":"070","slug":"confidence-intervals","term":"Uncertainty","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"confidence-intervals","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["survivorship-bias","zero-view-rate","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Uncertainty is part of the result.","dek":"An interval expresses uncertainty under a method’s assumptions.","point":"An interval expresses uncertainty under a method’s assumptions. It does not fix a poor sample, incomplete measurement or confounding.","body":["Before choosing a formula, identify the independent unit: post, account or campaign. Posts from one account may share common factors. Treating all of them as independent can look overly precise. Publish the method, assumptions and data beyond its reach.","Explain what the interval does not cover: collection errors, selection bias or a changed definition may sit outside its calculation. Readers should distinguish statistical uncertainty from overall measurement quality. This makes a result less dramatic but more useful when deciding whether to act or measure better. Numerical precision should not suppress the practical question of whether the underlying observations represent the population and outcome being discussed."],"action":["Define the unit of analysis.","Explain the method and assumptions."],"trap":"A narrow interval does not guarantee a properly framed causal question.","quote":"Uncertainty is part of the result.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Uncertainty is part of the result.","text":"An interval expresses uncertainty under a method’s assumptions.","media":"/images/editorial/confidence-intervals.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Uncertainty","text":"An interval expresses uncertainty under a method’s assumptions. It does not fix a poor sample, incomplete measurement or confounding.","media":"/images/editorial/confidence-intervals.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A narrow interval does not guarantee a properly framed causal question.","media":"/images/editorial/confidence-intervals.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define the unit of analysis.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/confidence-intervals.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Explain the method and assumptions.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/confidence-intervals.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/confidence-intervals.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"Mist drifts across a still mountain lake around the silhouette of a small tree."},"credit":"Bernd Thaller","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: abf225ea99a36441f354adb2bc92f24ea474854f.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Receding_Fog_over_Lake_Altaussee.jpg","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
23:["$","$L11","071",{"a":{"id":"071","slug":"survivorship-bias","term":"Survivorship bias","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"survivorship-bias","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["regression-to-mean","confidence-intervals","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"The missing accounts had results too.","dek":"Survivorship bias appears when analysis retains only still-visible units.","point":"Survivorship bias appears when analysis retains only still-visible units. A network evaluated without abandoned accounts can look artificially strong.","body":["Keep exit reasons and last observed dates. Separate intentionally stopped, inaccessible and uncollected accounts. Portfolio analysis should begin with an initial cohort and explain what happened to it. Surviving assets answer a different question from the original investment.","Show a small cohort-status table: still active, intentionally stopped, inaccessible and unknown. Categories should reflect verified facts and dates. This explains why counts decline and prevents strong survivor outcomes from being presented as returns across every account originally launched. Keep unknown states separate instead of assigning a convenient reason for disappearance. The incomplete history is itself a limitation of what the final performance comparison can claim."],"action":["Freeze the initial cohort.","Record exits and their costs."],"trap":"Lost data must not be invented; report the coverage limitation.","quote":"The missing accounts had results too.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"The missing accounts had results too.","text":"Survivorship bias appears when analysis retains only still-visible units.","media":"/images/editorial/survivorship-bias.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Survivorship bias","text":"Survivorship bias appears when analysis retains only still-visible units. A network evaluated without abandoned accounts can look artificially strong.","media":"/images/editorial/survivorship-bias.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Lost data must not be invented; report the coverage limitation.","media":"/images/editorial/survivorship-bias.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Freeze the initial cohort.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/survivorship-bias.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Record exits and their costs.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/survivorship-bias.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/survivorship-bias.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"The rusted hull of a shipwreck rests in the surf off a sandy beach."},"credit":"Ximonic (Simo Räsänen)","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 06bc209cac48bb2a2a4f1a66a004ae8a68c74102.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wreck_of_Cabo_de_Santa_Maria,_2010_December_-_4.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
24:["$","$L11","072",{"a":{"id":"072","slug":"regression-to-mean","term":"Regression to the mean","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"regression-to-mean","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["cohort-maturity","survivorship-bias","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"After a hit, returning to earth is not always a failure.","dek":"An extreme outcome can be followed by more ordinary outcomes.","point":"An extreme outcome can be followed by more ordinary outcomes. This possibility cautions against attributing every decline to the latest decision.","body":["After an exceptional post, compare subsequent output with the full history rather than the peak alone. Keep a change timeline. A new hook may coincide with a decline without causing it. Evaluating a change requires a suitable comparison, not the memory of the best day.","A review can show three references: the period before the hit, the hit itself and subsequent posts. This sometimes slows a premature diagnosis. It proves no cause, but reveals whether later results resemble ordinary activity more than an unprecedented collapse. Documented incidents still need separate investigation. The objective is to keep an exceptional observation from becoming the only standard against which every future post is judged."],"action":["Compare with a stable baseline.","Separate ordinary variation from verified incidents."],"trap":"This possible phenomenon should not be used to dismiss a real technical deterioration.","quote":"After a hit, returning to earth is not always a failure.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"After a hit, returning to earth is not always a failure.","text":"An extreme outcome can be followed by more ordinary outcomes.","media":"/images/editorial/regression-to-mean.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Regression to the mean","text":"An extreme outcome can be followed by more ordinary outcomes. This possibility cautions against attributing every decline to the latest decision.","media":"/images/editorial/regression-to-mean.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"This possible phenomenon should not be used to dismiss a real technical deterioration.","media":"/images/editorial/regression-to-mean.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Compare with a stable baseline.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/regression-to-mean.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Separate ordinary variation from verified incidents.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/regression-to-mean.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/regression-to-mean.jpg","width":1170,"height":1600,"alt":{"en":"An ornate antique pendulum clock with a white face and carved gold decoration."},"credit":"Christoph Braun","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: b886568db215861a1a91c3da842925a719a0dd4c.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pendulum_clock_by_Jacob_Kock,_antique_furniture_photography,_IMG_0931_edit.jpg","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en"}},"lang":"en"}]
25:["$","$L11","073",{"a":{"id":"073","slug":"cohort-maturity","term":"Cohort maturity","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"cohort-maturity","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["attribution","regression-to-mean","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Day seven does not exist for yesterday’s visitor.","dek":"Day-seven conversion should cover people given seven full days to convert.","point":"Day-seven conversion should cover people given seven full days to convert. Mixing mature and recent cohorts distorts comparisons.","body":["Define journey start and conversion. Compare cohorts at equal ages while showing missing data. Monthly purchases divided by monthly visits is not automatically a cohort conversion rate: buyers may have arrived long before the displayed window.","For daily cohorts, keep entry date and measurement cutoff. A table can show recent cohorts without calculating their final rate. This preserves visibility into new activity while protecting comparisons. Immature data is not bad data; it simply concerns a question whose full observation time has not elapsed. Make that distinction visible rather than silently including recent arrivals in a denominator they have not had time to complete."],"action":["Choose the starting event and outcome.","Exclude immature journeys from day-seven rates."],"trap":"A purchase during a period is not necessarily attributable to a visit in that period.","quote":"Day seven does not exist for yesterday’s visitor.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Day seven does not exist for yesterday’s visitor.","text":"Day-seven conversion should cover people given seven full days to convert.","media":"/images/editorial/cohort-maturity.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Cohort maturity","text":"Day-seven conversion should cover people given seven full days to convert. Mixing mature and recent cohorts distorts comparisons.","media":"/images/editorial/cohort-maturity.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A purchase during a period is not necessarily attributable to a visit in that period.","media":"/images/editorial/cohort-maturity.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Choose the starting event and outcome.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/cohort-maturity.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Exclude immature journeys from day-seven rates.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/cohort-maturity.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/cohort-maturity.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"A small tomato seedling pushes two green leaves above dry brown soil."},"credit":"Ksheera Piraati","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 4f0a3b5f6801bc6c97e59c31a53e6d0adbc51709.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Young_seedling_of_tomato_emerging_from_soil_-_India.jpg","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
26:["$","$L11","074",{"a":{"id":"074","slug":"attribution","term":"Attribution","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"attribution","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["views-to-buyers","cohort-maturity","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A UTM tells you about the click. Not the whole story.","dek":"Campaign parameters describe an instrumented origin.","point":"Campaign parameters describe an instrumented origin. They do not alone prove a piece of content caused a purchase decision.","body":["Keep first touch, last link and customer-declared source separate. A personal recommendation may precede a tagged visit. Do not erase that nuance in one number. Unattributed share remains unknown; it is neither failure nor hidden success to claim.","This publication’s TokPortal links carry an editorial source and article identifier. They help recognize some visits, not reconstruct every prior exposure. A reader may return without parameters or on another device. Reporting should state coverage and avoid treating identifiable visits as the entirety of influence. Equally, unattributed outcomes should not be claimed for the publication merely because its content could theoretically have contributed earlier in the journey."],"action":["Name each attribution view precisely.","Deduplicate buyers across content."],"trap":"Adding assisted conversions from several articles can count the same customer repeatedly.","quote":"A UTM tells you about the click. Not the whole story.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A UTM tells you about the click. Not the whole story.","text":"Campaign parameters describe an instrumented origin.","media":"/images/editorial/attribution.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Attribution","text":"Campaign parameters describe an instrumented origin. They do not alone prove a piece of content caused a purchase decision.","media":"/images/editorial/attribution.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Adding assisted conversions from several articles can count the same customer repeatedly.","media":"/images/editorial/attribution.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Name each attribution view precisely.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/attribution.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Deduplicate buyers across content.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/attribution.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/attribution.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"Several railway tracks branch and converge between signals and overhead lines."},"credit":"Jim.henderson","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 91b61c40a65e86a0dbd42d4884667e2ae8eee52b.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_Hills_Junction_tracks_jeh.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
27:["$","$L11","075",{"a":{"id":"075","slug":"views-to-buyers","term":"Views to buyers","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"views-to-buyers","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["experiment-preregistration","attribution","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A million views can miss the problem.","dek":"Views measure exposure under the platform’s definition.","point":"Views measure exposure under the platform’s definition. New buyers measure a separate commercial outcome requiring its own definition and source.","body":["Track movement from content to visit, use and purchase without assuming everyone is identifiable. For first purchases, exclude renewals and tests under documented rules. More views may still support awareness; they should not be renamed customer growth.","An article can support several goals: understanding, operator recruitment or product discovery. Define which one is being evaluated before rewriting its CTA. A page without directly attributed purchases may still provide real value. The trap is confusing that possible value with an already demonstrated commercial outcome. Keep each objective and evidence source separate so useful recruitment or learning paths are not erased by an overly narrow sales metric."],"action":["Define the intended commercial outcome.","Retain identity-matching limitations."],"trap":"An opened checkout or preview is not a real payment.","quote":"A million views can miss the problem.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A million views can miss the problem.","text":"Views measure exposure under the platform’s definition.","media":"/images/editorial/views-to-buyers.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Views to buyers","text":"Views measure exposure under the platform’s definition. New buyers measure a separate commercial outcome requiring its own definition and source.","media":"/images/editorial/views-to-buyers.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"An opened checkout or preview is not a real payment.","media":"/images/editorial/views-to-buyers.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define the intended commercial outcome.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/views-to-buyers.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Retain identity-matching limitations.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/views-to-buyers.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/views-to-buyers.jpg","width":1023,"height":680,"alt":{"en":"People move through a crowded night market in Kenting."},"credit":"Guess Tsai@flickr","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 3538298b12dbad52a12cca4548073dcb7c69fb22.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crowd_at_the_Kenting_Night_Market_20100925.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
28:["$","$L11","076",{"a":{"id":"076","slug":"experiment-preregistration","term":"Preregistration","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"experiment-preregistration","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["stop-rules","views-to-buyers","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Write possible verdicts before knowing the score.","dek":"Preregistering means recording an experiment’s question, criteria and planned analysis in advance.","point":"Preregistering means recording an experiment’s question, criteria and planned analysis in advance. It limits stories reconstructed after observation.","body":["A dated document is enough to begin: hypothesis, groups, duration, primary metric, exclusions and expected decision. You can modify the plan when reality demands it, provided the previous version and explanation remain. Exploration is still possible; label it as exploration.","Add an acceptable conclusion for each outcome: favorable signal, uncertain difference or measurement failure. This often exposes protocols that have no response to negative results. A useful experiment should remain informative when it contradicts the initial plan. Otherwise it mainly produces retrospective justification. Recording these possibilities also helps reviewers distinguish the intended decision from additional questions discovered while the experiment was already underway."],"action":["Freeze a plan version before collection.","Log departures and exploratory analyses."],"trap":"Preregistering a poor protocol does not validate it; it makes its choices visible.","quote":"Write possible verdicts before knowing the score.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Write possible verdicts before knowing the score.","text":"Preregistering means recording an experiment’s question, criteria and planned analysis in advance.","media":"/images/editorial/experiment-preregistration.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Preregistration","text":"Preregistering means recording an experiment’s question, criteria and planned analysis in advance. It limits stories reconstructed after observation.","media":"/images/editorial/experiment-preregistration.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"Preregistering a poor protocol does not validate it; it makes its choices visible.","media":"/images/editorial/experiment-preregistration.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Freeze a plan version before collection.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/experiment-preregistration.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Log departures and exploratory analyses.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/experiment-preregistration.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/experiment-preregistration.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"Gloved hands write experimental observations in an open laboratory notebook."},"credit":"Katherine Stember","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: ccc145165e1317324120da4f6b9bea5c40079bd7.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lab_Notebook.jpg","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
29:["$","$L11","077",{"a":{"id":"077","slug":"stop-rules","term":"Stop rules","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"stop-rules","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["evidence-ladder","experiment-preregistration","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"Knowing when to stop is part of the test.","dek":"A stop rule specifies when to end, pause or reconsider an experiment.","point":"A stop rule specifies when to end, pause or reconsider an experiment. It should account for expected information and operational constraints.","body":["Set a duration limit and incidents requiring a pause: missing data, wrong assets, changed scope. Stopping as soon as a number looks attractive can select favorable noise. Continuing indefinitely until success appears is no better method.","A pause for an incorrect file should preserve valid observations and identify affected posts. Do not automatically merge results before and after correction. Depending on the change, continue, restart part of the test or accept a limited conclusion. The stop rule protects interpretation as well as budget. Record who made the decision and why so a later reviewer can understand whether the final dataset still answers the original question."],"action":["Define deadline and pause criteria.","Separate operational stopping from statistical conclusions."],"trap":"An interrupted experiment need not have a verdict; it may simply be incomplete.","quote":"Knowing when to stop is part of the test.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"Knowing when to stop is part of the test.","text":"A stop rule specifies when to end, pause or reconsider an experiment.","media":"/images/editorial/stop-rules.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Stop rules","text":"A stop rule specifies when to end, pause or reconsider an experiment. It should account for expected information and operational constraints.","media":"/images/editorial/stop-rules.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"An interrupted experiment need not have a verdict; it may simply be incomplete.","media":"/images/editorial/stop-rules.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Define deadline and pause criteria.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/stop-rules.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Separate operational stopping from statistical conclusions.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/stop-rules.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/stop-rules.jpg","width":1280,"height":853,"alt":{"en":"A rusted railway buffer and heavy bolts beside a moss-covered wooden sleeper."},"credit":"Dietmar Rabich","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: b4d1327c14b2b9518d0812daf4f9dc941fcdf629.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haltern_am_See,_Sythen,_ehemalige_Bahnstrecke_--_2022_--_9807.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
2a:["$","$L11","078",{"a":{"id":"078","slug":"evidence-ladder","term":"Evidence ladder","category":"lab","kind":"protocol","image":"evidence-ladder","tier":"operating","evidence":"hypothesis","sources":[],"related":["viral-hit","stop-rules","distribution-is-the-moat"],"en":{"title":"A hypothesis needs a label, not a disguise.","dek":"The AGD evidence ladder separates platform documentation, methodical proprietary data, controlled experiments, repeated observations, hypotheses and folklore.","point":"The AGD evidence ladder separates platform documentation, methodical proprietary data, controlled experiments, repeated observations, hypotheses and folklore. Every claim should retain provenance.","body":["Documentation may confirm a feature exists without proving its effect on reach. Internal observation may reveal a pattern without establishing a cause. Write the exact proposition supported by each source. Evidence level belongs to the claim, not author prestige or the number of links below it.","During review, underline verbs asserting a cause: increases, reduces, causes. Ask what evidence supports each one. A descriptive rewrite may be more accurate: a difference is observed and its cause remains unknown. This sentence-level work is more useful than a global “data-driven” badge above the article. Readers need to know which proposition a source actually supports, especially when one paragraph combines documented features with untested performance hypotheses."],"action":["Attach a source or label to each claim.","Keep unmeasured effects unknown."],"trap":"A promotional source does not become independent because another publication cites it.","quote":"A hypothesis needs a label, not a disguise.","stories":[{"id":"brief","title":"The idea in three screens.","slides":[{"label":"THE SIGNAL","title":"A hypothesis needs a label, not a disguise.","text":"The AGD evidence ladder separates platform documentation, methodical proprietary data, controlled experiments, repeated observations, hypotheses and folklore.","media":"/images/editorial/evidence-ladder.jpg"},{"label":"THE CONCEPT","title":"Evidence ladder","text":"The AGD evidence ladder separates platform documentation, methodical proprietary data, controlled experiments, repeated observations, hypotheses and folklore. Every claim should retain provenance.","media":"/images/editorial/evidence-ladder.jpg"},{"label":"THE OTHER SIDE","title":"What can mislead.","text":"A promotional source does not become independent because another publication cites it.","media":"/images/editorial/evidence-ladder.jpg"}]},{"id":"practice","title":"From concept to practice.","slides":[{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 1","title":"Attach a source or label to each claim.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/evidence-ladder.jpg"},{"label":"PUT IT TO WORK / 2","title":"Keep unmeasured effects unknown.","text":"Adapt this to your audience, budget and test scope.","media":"/images/editorial/evidence-ladder.jpg"}]}]},"schemaVersion":1,"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T12:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T17:06:44.287Z","author":"feedraid-editorial","media":{"kind":"photograph","src":"/images/editorial/evidence-ladder.jpg","width":1080,"height":607,"alt":{"en":"Rough stone steps climb between large rocks and green plants."},"credit":"RedRyan101","provenance":"Wikimedia Commons photograph. Resized and JPEG-compressed from the source photograph. Original source SHA1: 94a102430cb60ab7c908d2ed9ea3509f3b61f39f.","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stone_stairs.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0"}},"lang":"en"}]
